    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01BZHwSgnGAC4LTh4wgvYJsE?thread=cmsg_01BZHwSgnGAC4LTh4wgvYJsEJednwGwKMDB1BiJTjNfxLK)_\n\n`main` currently fails two checks, and so does every PR that merges it, #171 among them.\n\n**`markers`**: the merge in deb409e left git conflict markers in `sp-org-tag-registry.el`. The fix keeps `main`'s grouped layout from ADR 0020 and puts the two tags added in 770391d, `plugin` and `workflow`, into `sp-org-tag-groups-ungrouped`, above the `sp-org-tag-add` marker line.\n\n**`tangle`**: the same merge removed the `counsel-recoll` functions from `sp-search.el`, but it kept the `R` \"Recoll\" entry in the transient menu, which `sp-search.org` no longer has. I re-tangled the file from the doc, and that drops the entry.\n\nLocally, `check-conflict-markers.sh` and `check-tangle.sh` both pass. I haven't loaded either file in a full Emacs config.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BTsYhS2AiM2jwu2CYD5nMu",
